{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The bars of Sheol.</b> Like the branches of Sheol by way of parable, as though Sheol is a tree below, like: \"and he made bars\" (Exodus 26:26). And it should have been אל בדי שאול תרדנה (to the bars of Sheol they will go down); or ישוב תרדנה על בדי (they will again go down upon the bars) — for בדי שאול תפולנה ותרדנה (the bars of Sheol, they will fall and go down) — and as though man is upon the branches of Sheol." "<b>Go down.</b> Some say: ירד or נחת, as its meaning, for יַחַד יֵשׁ לָנוּ עֲלֵי עָפָר נָחַת (together we have rest upon the dust)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Exodus 26:26 (וְעָשִׂיתָ בְרִיחֵי); his ותעש בדים may reflect a variant reading or loose citation.", 1 "The first verb (ירד or נחת) relates to the preceding form in v. 16; the rest is a quotation of Job 17:16 (or a parallel form of it), left untranslated as it is a quoted Hebrew form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:59.414387499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}